# package.use for the INSTALLER profile only (plan/16, plan/21).
#
# Files named profile.<name> in this directory are copied into the config root by stage 20 only
# when that profile is the one being built; every other file here is shared by all of them. USE
# is resolved once per package, so a flag that one image needs and another must not have has
# nowhere else to live.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dev-qt/qttools[linguist] — required to BUILD the installer page, not to run it.
#
# <id>-calamares-accounts (config/portage/overlay) is a Calamares view module built out of
# tree against the installed Calamares, because Calamares accepts only C++ QtPlugin view
# modules (plan/21 §2). Building out of tree means find_package(Calamares), and the exported
# CalamaresConfig.cmake opens with:
#
#     set(qt_required Core Widgets LinguistTools)
#     find_package(${qtname} CONFIG REQUIRED ${qt_required})
#
# LinguistTools is hardcoded into the REQUIRED component list every consumer of the Calamares
# CMake package inherits, whether or not that consumer ships a translation. This one has
# translatable strings — tr() in the C++, qsTr() in the QML — but no .ts files and no catalog,
# so it needs the CMake package and never invokes lrelease. The cmake package
# /usr/lib64/cmake/Qt6LinguistTools is gated on this USE flag, so with it off the module
# fails at configure time with
#
#     Failed to find required Qt component "LinguistTools"
#
# and the installer page cannot be built at all. Confirmed by configuring the module against the
# real installed 3.4.2, not inferred from the ebuild.
#
# The flag costs no packages anywhere: qttools' linguist? RDEPEND is a lone
# "widgets? ( !dev-qt/linguist:5 )" slot blocker, so no lock gains an atom — only qttools' own
# contents grow, and only on this profile.
#
# It does also build the Qt Linguist GUI, which has no audience on an installer medium either.
# USE has no move that keeps Qt6LinguistTools for the build while dropping the app from the
# image, so the app is deleted after the merge instead: stage 50 section 3h, which asserts it
# stays gone. That is the same treatment, for the same reason, that section 3g gives the Qt
# D-Bus Viewer — see the long note in package.use/image about qdbus and widgets.
dev-qt/qttools                    linguist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kde-apps/thumbnailers[-pdf] is GONE (plan/34 §6, was plan/20 §4.2).
#
# Through 0.3.1 this dropped the Ghostscript chain — six packages, 96.0 MiB installed, serving
# one Dolphin PDF/PostScript thumbnailer — from the installer medium only, on the judgement that
# nobody browses a PDF library on a stick that boots once to run Calamares. That judgement is
# sound; what changed is that it is no longer one this file gets to make. plan/34 §3 turns the
# installer's tail into a systemd system extension built as a DIFFERENCE against the desktop's
# tree, and dropping a USE flag the desktop has is a REMOVAL relative to that tree — the same
# shape as the `#not-live` markers plan/34 §6 also removed, just through package.use instead of
# a set file. The installer tree has to be the desktop's plus a tail, at identical versions, so
# this profile now resolves `pdf` exactly like the desktop does and the whole chain (ghostscript,
# its fonts, poppler-data, the orphans the resolver used to drop with it) is back.
